    docs(CF-186): the arm census CF-155 shipped no longer exists — re-pin the count, add the two missing table rows, file the restoration
    
    The acceptance plan claimed tests/selftest.sh carries "37 sections ... plus
    three lettered sub-arms, §4b, §7b and §7c ... so the tree carries 40 arms", and
    stated that §7c runs the section census green on the tree and red on a fixture
    with one extra numbered section. The total is now right by accident: §7c does
    not exist, and the three lettered arms it can see are §4b, §7b and §31b.
    
    §7c is gone. CF-155 shipped it at 32f38a5 (`git show 32f38a5:tests/selftest.sh
    | grep -cE '^say "§?[0-9]+[a-z]\.'` = 3). The CF-151 landing 4ce1e48 descends
    from that commit (`git merge-base --is-ancestor 32f38a5 4ce1e48` = 0) and
    rewrote tests/selftest.sh from a copy that predated §7c while adding §37, so the
    arm was dropped by a stale full-file copy rather than by a decision. At the
    parent tip 7ec7137 `grep -c cf155 tests/selftest.sh` = 0 and `bash
    tests/selftest.sh` still prints SELFTEST: PASS with 139 PASS rows and zero cf155
    rows — the deletion is invisible to the suite, so the census is a diagnostic
    again until the arm is restored.
    
    The reverse-mapping table promised to name every arm and did not, in two ways
    counted mechanically rather than read: at 7ec7137 it carried 38 ids against 40
    arms with §36 (CF-159, landed at 8b81369) and §31b (CF-183, landed at 5069c0a
    while this tick was rebasing over it) both missing. The same page also
    contradicted itself: the current-state line said 40 arms while the reverse
    paragraph said "Twelve of the 39 arms". The tree carries 37 numbered sections
    plus §4b, §7b and §31b.
    
    This commit is docs + board only:
    - docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md: current-state line re-measured at 7ec7137
      (2026-11-04T09:22Z, UTC) — 37 sections, three lettered arms, 40 arms, 139 PASS
      rows, board 159 rows / 320 events, all pinned to the one tip they were measured
      on; the false §7c gate claim replaced with the measured deletion and its
      restoring row; the reverse paragraph corrected from "Twelve of the 39" to "of
      the 40", from "remaining 27 / each is governed" to "remaining 28, of which 15
      carry a governing row and 13 do not" (CF-113 owns that exhaustiveness claim);
      §36 and §31b added to the mapping table.
    - .coding-hermes/board: CF-186 filed (P3, pending) with a paste-runnable probe
      that prints `lettered=3 cf155_rows=0 suite=PASS` from the repository root, and
      acceptance criteria that require the arm back with both gate directions
      executed and a lettered-arm census that makes the next deletion decidable.
    
    Verified at the rebased tree: `bash docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh` -> rc
    0, `measured: tip=7ec7137 rows=159 events=320 sections=37` / `OK: milestone,
    plan snapshot and layer arms agree at 7ec7137`; `bash tests/selftest.sh` -> rc 0,
    `SELFTEST: PASS`, 139 PASS / 19 intentional fixture FAIL rows; `bash
    scripts/boardctl validate` -> `RESULT: OK (3 warning(s))` (the two CF-034
    free-form fields plus the headerless board, all pre-existing). The pre-fix state
    reproduces from the parent tree: the same table census gives `arms=40
    table_ids=38 missing_from_table: 31b 36`, and the page claims both 39 and 40.
    
    Sibling disclosure: nine commits landed on origin/main while this tick measured
    (the clone was taken at 69a08f1, the rebase landed over 7ec7137). §31b/CF-183 is
    one of them; it is named in the table here rather than filed as a gap by this
    lane. The event log conflict was resolved by keeping all five sibling events and
    renumbering this tick's task_created to 321 (`dup_ids=0`, `cf186_lines=1`).
    
    Hook position, stated rather than assumed: this commit was made in a fresh
    scratch clone of origin/main, where `git config --get core.hooksPath` is empty
    and `.git/hooks/pre-commit` does not exist — so no hook ran and none was
    bypassed. The Tier-1 reading comes from the explicit `gitreins task complete`
    run for CF-186-PM1 after the push, which refuses this diff shape as a DEGRADED
    PASS in a hooked checkout.
    
